The Pangea desktop app carries this folder as source, and the plugins it builds on your Mac are
built from it. Conduit AI also publishes it, with the desktop app, as a public repository; the
app's About section gives its address.

Parts by another author

The Felt look in platform/web (the Felt parts of pangea.css, pangea.js, mapping.js, host.js,
builder.js and harmony.js, as the first line of each says) and six examples (the whole of the
logic.cpp of examples/bass-and-drums, hands-and-drums, pocket-drums, ostinato-hands,
rolling-line and two-hands, with two-hands' README.md and test folder) are not Conduit AI's
code. Since 25 November 2026 their author offers them, as they are in this folder, under the GNU
Affero General Public License, version 3 or later, as well as under his own licence, at your
choice: platform/web/FELT-LICENSE.md has both, and each of the six logic.cpp says so. Five of
them also carry the MIDI shelf's licence line, which names library/midi/LICENSE.md, in Pangea's
own repository only; its text is the first part of platform/web/FELT-LICENSE.md. So all the code
in this folder may be used under the GNU Affero General Public License.

